      "content_fixes": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "old": "King Solomon was lowkey obsessed with women. It wasn't just Pharaoh's daughter; he had a whole squad of foreign wives—from Moab, Ammon, Edom, Sidon, and the Hittites. These were the exact nations God had warned Israel about, saying, 'Don't you dare marry them, or they'll get you hooked on their sketchy gods.' But Solomon, being extra, fell hard for them and just couldn't let them go. He had 700 wives who were basically royalty and another 300 side-chicks. A thousand women! And yeah, they totally turned his heart away from God. As he got older, his wives played him, getting him into their foreign gods, and he wasn't loyal to his God anymore, not like his dad David had been. He started worshipping Ashtoreth, the goddess of the Sidonians, and Molech, the super messed-up god of the Ammonites.",
          "new": "King Solomon was lowkey obsessed with women. It wasn't just Pharaoh's daughter; he had a whole squad of foreign wives—from Moab, Ammon, Edom, Sidon, and the Hittites. These were the exact nations God had warned Israel about, saying, 'Don't you dare marry them, or they'll get you hooked on their sketchy gods.' But Solomon, being extra, fell hard for them and just couldn't let them go. He had 700 wives who were basically royalty and another 300 concubines. A thousand women! And yeah, they totally turned his heart away from God. As he got older, his wives played him, getting him into their foreign gods, and he wasn't loyal to his God anymore, not like his dad David had been. He started worshipping Ashtoreth, the goddess of the Sidonians, and Molech, the super messed-up god of the Ammonites.",
          "reason": "\"side-chicks\" is crude sexual slang for concubines; MSG says \"three hundred concubines\"."
        }
      ],
      "flagged": [],
      "ok": false
    },
