      "content_fixes": [
        {
          "index": 13,
          "old": "It was during Ahab's rule that a guy named Hiel from Bethel rebuilt the city of Jericho, but it came at a crazy cost. He lost his oldest son, Abiram, when they laid the foundation, and his youngest son, Segub, when they set up the gates. This was the exact fulfillment of what Joshua, son of Nun, had prophesied would happen.",
          "new": "It was during Ahab's rule that a guy named Hiel from Bethel rebuilt the city of Jericho, but it came at a crazy cost. He sacrificed his oldest son, Abiram, when they laid the foundation, and his youngest son, Segub, when they set up the gates. This was the exact fulfillment of what Joshua, son of Nun, had prophesied would happen.",
